"NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090", "vram_size": 32187}, "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "226827293", "author": {"steamid": "76561198883107762", "personaname": "Shaykaye", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/shaykaye/", "num_games_owned": 524, "num_reviews": 37, "playtime_forever": 271, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 271, "last_played": 1780191580, "avatar": "6a214791e0b467c0fe1d556441f5b3ad1230040c"}, "language": "english", "review": "I don't have many words for this game man, It feels like a slog to even write this review. \n\nIt gets boring really fast even if you have a dedicated party. I’m currently sitting at the start of act 2 and I honestly don’t have the willpower to push any further. Does that mean that the game and it's mechanics are bad? Not at all. The weapon play and movement are very fluid, the animations for the guns are pretty nice sometimes, the recoil feels good, the melee... passes. I just think the problem is that after about 20 minutes reality starts to set in and you’re sat there thinking, like “why the ♥♥♥♥ am I playing this?”. I picked it up for like 5$. I'm not that pressed over five bucks. But it being sold for 60$ at one point. That's insane.\n\nHonestly the worst thing about games like this is that they're mediocre. Not bad. just OKAY. And you can waste your time on OKAY. You shouldn't, but you can. You know what you can't waste time on? You can't waste time on something that's just bad. And I think this game has made me appreciate bad games.\n", "timestamp_created": 1780192238, "timestamp_updated": 1780192709, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "226819323", "author": {"steamid": "76561198383044849", "person